Well I did it. After coming so close last week with a different
Valkyrie, only to die on the Astral Plane, I did it this time.

It was a pretty standard game for me, except that I switched my
strategy a couple of weeks back to use Excalibur as my primary weapon
instead of Mjollnir. Since Excalibur has auto-search and prevents
level drain, I found that I was switching to it so much, that Mjollnir
wasn't doing much for me.

This game I never even found Gauntlets of Power so using Mjollnir as a
ranged weapon wasn't even an option.

Found an altar on DLvl 2 and converted it. Went into the mines found a
co-aligned altar in Minetown (rare thing for me lately). Somewhere
around Minetown I found a polymorph trap (thank you Excalibur for
letting me not find it the hard way). I went back up, found a dog,
went down and polymorphed him a few times until I got an orange
dragon. I was happy with that so I took him around for a while and let
him level up on my way down to the wine cellar. Got the luckstone and
the potions and headed back up to Minetown with a pretty good pet
dragon. He took out most of the shopkeepers so I cleaned them out,
bought what protection I could and headed back up to the dungeon. I
still had no bag of holding at this time, so I had to leave a bunch of
stuff in a chest next to the altar for now.

Went and cleared out Sokoban and got an amulet of reflection. Could
have used a bag right then, but I never complain about getting the
amulet that early - especially if you see my YAAD post from a couple
of weeks ago - reflection is my best friend lately.

Anyway, kept going down, only had a few scares. Either a chameleon or
a real lich popped up right under my nose on one level, but my dragon
quickly dispatched him cause he caught himself in a spider web (lucky
me). Finally found a bag of holding somewhere along the way and set up
show in a co-aligned temple of DLvl 16. This was primary base camp for
most of the rest of the game. I didn't have any levitation yet, so I
figured I'd do the quest and see what goodies I could collect down
there.

The quest was pretty uneventful, except that I took a misstep in Lord
Surtur's lair and ended up in the lava, thus putting an end to my
beloved speed boots. I thought I was screwed at this point because
here I am stuck in the lava, not knowing how to get out. I zapped a
wand of cold (at myself first in a panic, and then down) to cool the
lava, but I was still stuck. Luckily a zap of teleportation wand freed
me.

Dispatched Surtur and made my way back up. ID'd a bunch of stuff and
found out that I really didn't have anything good. I had a +5 Dwarvish
Cloak and a +4 or +5 Elven Leather Helm. Those were the two good
pieces that I had. And with no speed boots, I needed some help.

I found Ludios and me and the dragon went and cleared it out. Killed a
gray dragon in there, but no scales. Since I had already found two
huge leprechaun halls earlier, I didn't need the gold, I was just
looking for equipment, but I think all I ended up with that was useful
was a wand of death off one of the soldiers.

Somewhere along the way I got some water walking boots so I made my
way down to Medusa's island. It was the one with the Titan, but being
Lawful, he was peaceful (so glad). Anyway the dragon made short work
of him anyway. Went across, stoned Medusa chopped up the statues and
got Levitation boots. Went down two levels to the castle and while I'm
standing on the upstairs, I've got a Master Lich staring me in the
face. Panic sets in, but I'm calm enough to just go back up and
regroup. I was still only wearing a dwarvish cloak and elven mithril.
If he had TODed me, I would have not been happy. Another lich along
the way back up disintegrated my helmet. I hadn't found any scrolls of
genocide yet, so I was starting to worry. No MR, no genocide scrolls.
Not good.

One level above the castle was an altar so I hung around and
sacrificed for a long time. At least two and maybe 3 gray dragons
appeared but never left me any scales (greedy buzzards). I finally
just nutted up and went down to face the lich with my dragon. I
figured if I got toasted, oh well, try again. Since I was on the
upstairs, he just danced around me throwing curses and wasting turns
going invisible and speeding up and the like. Me and the dragon
finished him off with not so much as a scratch. Cleared the castle, at
which point the dragon bought it. He must have been weakened from the
Lich. Proceeded to clear out and kill two silver dragons, one yielding
scales (yay!). I already had reflection, but at least I could get some
better AC. The castle had the wand (of course), speed boots (thank
Tyr), and a cloak of protection.

Wished for cloak of magic resistance, scrolls of charging and a scroll
of genocide. Genocided mind flayers, master mind flayers and blessed
genocided Liches. Tried my first hand at alchemy and mixed up like 30
something potions of full healing. Got HP up to over 400 and went down
into Gehennom. No trouble here except in the Santuary. Got double
Rodneys who proceeded to summon up a shitstorm of baddies. Had to use
a cockatrice corpse to stone each and every one that I could
(including both Wizards). Got the amulet, got my stolen property back
and got out of Dodge. Had some problems with the Force and the Wizard
kept coming back. I never did figure out how to ditch him on a level
and never see him again (oh well).

The planes were no problem; spent a little longer on Fire than I would
have liked but couldn't find the portal. I know there is a trick, but
I don't know it, so I didn't bother getting spoiled on that part.
Astral plane was actually quite easy this time. Being unburded must
have been the key. When I made it here last week, I was killing
Pestilence and Death and Famine over and over, getting Ill, Hungry,
etc. Last week I blew through 3 amulets of life saving before I died.
This time, I had 3 amulets and a wand of wishing and 10 potions of
full healing, but I don't think I had to use any!! Of course my luck,
I chose the wrong altar the first two times and had to traverse the
whole map to finally get the right one.

I don't know how to dump out the log file like everyone does, so I'll
just say that my end-game stats were nothing special. Death drained my
HP down to 300-ish from the 400+ that I had before leaving the
dungeon. I killed each of the Astral Plane bosses multiple times.
Killed the stupid Wizard 15 times before I could get out of the
dungeons. Geryon and Yeenoghu were summoned and dispatched and that
was about it.

